    {
      "text": "whoso shall publish peace, 1 Ne. 13:37. had thy peace been as a river, 1 Ne. 20:18. that which shall be written … establishing peace among the fruit of thy loins, 2 Ne. 3:12. why should I give way to temptations, that the evil one … destroy my peace, 2 Ne. 4:27. have peace with him, until three generations, 2 Ne. 26:9. by laboring … did once more establish peace, W of M 1:18 (Mosiah 29:14; 4 Ne. 1:4). having peace of conscience, Mosiah 4:3. not have a mind to injure one another, but to live peaceably, Mosiah 4:13. founder of peace … the Lord, Mosiah 15:18. let no pride nor haughtiness disturb their peace, Mosiah 27:4. Melchizedek did establish peace, Alma 13:18. buried the weapons of war, for peace, Alma 24:19. deliver up your weapons of war and depart with a covenant of peace, Alma 44:14. In memory of our God … and our peace, Alma 46:12. no contention in the land, because of the love of God, 4 Ne. 1:15.",
